@startuml seq_dia_programming_refused
title SC-DIA-04 - Programming session refused by the application

participant "UDS tester" as Tester
participant "Plant model" as Plant
participant "TCU" as TCU

note over Tester, TCU
Covers: SYS-DIA-004, SYS-DIA-002, SIM-TST-002, SIM-TST-004, SG-05
UDS requests on DIAG_PhysReq 0x7E1, responses on DIAG_Resp 0x7E9 (can_matrix section 5).
CAN frames pass can0 / slcand / gateway transparently (DC-05, SIM-GW-001), see SC-STA-04.
end note

note over TCU: control active, default session; the tester runs beside the plant model (SIM-TST-004)
loop every 10 ms
  Plant -> TCU : SIM_Driver, SIM_Speed, SIM_Analog
end

Tester -> TCU : 10 02
TCU --> Tester : 7F 10 7E
note right: 10 02 only from the extended session\n(reprogramming section 3)

Tester -> TCU : 10 03
TCU --> Tester : 50 03 00 32 01 F4
Tester -> TCU : 31 01 02 03
TCU --> Tester : 71 01 02 03 <result>
note right: checkProgrammingPreconditions: 00 = OK, else bit 0 not at standstill,\nbit 1 not in P, bit 2 speed invalid (reprogramming section 11);\nexample at 20 km/h in D: 71 01 02 03 03

alt vehicle moving (>= 2 km/h, e.g. 20 km/h)
  Plant -> TCU : SIM_Speed: OutputShaftSpeed of 20 km/h
  Tester -> TCU : 10 02
  TCU --> Tester : 7F 10 22
else selector not P
  Plant -> TCU : SIM_Driver: Selector = 1, 2 or 3
  Tester -> TCU : 10 02
  TCU --> Tester : 7F 10 22
else vehicle speed invalid
  Plant -> TCU : SIM_Speed: OutputShaftSpeed > 8000 rpm, or SIM_Speed timeout
  Tester -> TCU : 10 02
  TCU --> Tester : 7F 10 22
end
note right of TCU: conditionsNotCorrect (SYS-DIA-004)
TCU -> TCU : stays in the application, extended session; control continues
note over Tester, TCU: Safe state of SG-05: the programming request is rejected. Accepted case: SC-BOOT-01 step 5.
@enduml
